{"name":"Cigar","hex":"#7d4e38","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cigar","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cylinder of tobacco rolled and wrapped with an outer covering of tobacco leaves, intended to be smoked.","The penis. (Can we add an example for this sense?)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cigar"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cigar","blocks":[{"text":"A cigar is a rolled bundle of dried and fermented tobacco leaves made to be smoked. Cigars are produced in a variety of sizes and shapes. Since the 20th century, almost all cigars are made of three distinct components: the filler, the binder leaf which holds the filler together, and a wrapper leaf, which is often the highest quality leaf used. Often there will be a cigar band printed with the cigar manufacturer's logo. Modern cigars can come with two or more bands, especially Cuban cigars, showing Limited Edition bands displaying the year of production."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Cigar_tube_and_cutter.jpg/330px-Cigar_tube_and_cutter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cigar"},{"title":"Cigar (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Cigar, was an American Thoroughbred racehorse who was the 1995 and 1996 American Horse of the Year. He was the first American racehorse racing against top-class competition to win 16 consecutive races since Triple Crown winner Citation did so between 1948 and 1950. His major wins included the 1995 Breeders' Cup Classic, the NYRA Mile, Jockey Club Gold Cup, Woodward Stakes (twice), Oaklawn Handicap, Hollywood Gold Cup, Donn Handicap (twice) and the first running of the Dubai World Cup. He became the leading money earner in racing history and was later inducted into the National Museum of Racing and Hall of Fame."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Heads_Up_CigarJPG.jpg/330px-Heads_Up_CigarJPG.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cigar_(horse)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/MuseoRegionalTuxtla_27.JPG/500px-MuseoRegionalTuxtla_27.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/MuseoRegionalTuxtla_27.JPG/1280px-MuseoRegionalTuxtla_27.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/MuseoRegionalTuxtla_27.JPG/500px-MuseoRegionalTuxtla_27.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Indigenous tobacco pipe on display at the regional museum in San Andrés Tuxtla, Mexico","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMuseoRegionalTuxtla_27.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1b/Harrynelsonpillsbury.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1b/Harrynelsonpillsbury.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Harry Nelson Pillsbury smoking a cigar","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHarrynelsonpillsbury.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Ybor_Cigar_workers.jpg/500px-Ybor_Cigar_workers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Ybor_Cigar_workers.jpg/500px-Ybor_Cigar_workers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Inside an Ybor City cigar factory c. 1920","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AYbor_Cigar_workers.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Cigar_making_display%2C_Ybor_City_Museum_State_Park%2C_Tampa%2C_Florida.jpg/500px-Cigar_making_d